{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"01f4100c6dabf72cb5f905875be68734e4103afa79e76b1414237170742927db","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / rich_text_cutover","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py::_load_module","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py::test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas","sys.modules","rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf","AdfCodec","rich_text_codec.py","test_by_path_loader_preserves_module_identity","_marklas","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py"],"problem_keywords":["test isolation","module state leak","sys.modules cache","test ordering dependency","serial full-suite failure"],"propositions":["The integration fixture _load_module unconditionally replaces sys.modules with a fresh module object, breaking the canonical-key/module-identity invariant required by test infrastructure.","AdfCodec retains a stale reference to the prior module object and calls its functions directly, causing a mismatch when the fixture installs a distinct module object.","Serial test ordering exposes the leak: when test_reconcile_roundtrip runs before test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas, the codec sees rich output while the test sees plain output because they observe different module identities.","The fix caches and returns the module when both canonical name and __file__ match the requested source, preserving same-source identity while allowing different-source replacement."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787807115161749001,"uuid":"bba705dc-9a0c-427d-9d3e-5068da4a0d9a"}